# Club & Grub - Book II ending: "The Long Raft Home" (designer D9b, Book II "The Far Shore").
# The playable credits (DESIGN.md A.2 / A.6, GAMEPLAY.md 13.1; difficulty 2, Expert only, no enemy): Grub floats home
# on one log raft with rails (objects/raft rails: a rider never leaves it) on a gentle current of 1 px per tick (about
# two minutes; paddling - a forward strike - halves the trip). He starts on the Roc's broken hoard, crouches on the
# hatch planks of its jetty to drop aboard and strikes towards the shore to push off. The credits ride past on
# floating signs at reading speed, food rains from the hoard, and the five islands of the Far Shore pass behind the
# raft - the red mesa, the tar delta's mangrove, the coral sea stacks, the idol isle and the storm spire. No cell in the
# raft's row before the beach, no vine. The current rests in a calm pool under the rock arch at the spire's foot (a
# sign says so): the raft stops there until a rider paddles on, so the high strikes at the big spot in the arch's
# underside, 3 rows over the water, never leave a hopping rider behind - three of them drop Cave Painting 19 (missing
# it fails nothing). The raft stops at the home beach; the welcome totem stands on a jetty plank over the last
# water, where every rider touches it: the tally, then THE END (the cave mural when all 30 paintings are found), the
# credits and the title.

[meta]
format = 2
id = ending_b
name = "The Long Raft Home"
kind = ending
order = 0
book = 2
world = 0
stage = 0
biome = village
terrain_a = coast/terrain_sand
terrain_b = jungle/terrain_grass
background = coast
music = ending_raft
liquid = water
min_difficulty = expert
password_expert = "RAFT"
bonus_tier = 2
author = D9b

